  "definition": {
   "definition": "Notes in circulation comprises currency notes issued by the Government of India up to 1935 and by the Reserve Bank since then, less notes held in the Banking Department of the Bank — that is, notes held outside the RBI by the public, banks and treasuries (Government of India one-rupee notes issued since July 1940 are treated as rupee coins and excluded from this head). It is a liability of the Issue Department, where total notes issued = notes in circulation + notes held in the Banking Department, and is published weekly in the WSS 'Reserve Bank of India — Liabilities and Assets' table (item 1).",
